          "node": {
            "body": "\u003cp\u003eWhat a challenge it is to launch a browser nowadays! Why did you take that bet instead of building a Chrome extension? How are people reacting to the change?\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAll the best for the launch!\u003c/p\u003e",
            "createdAt": "2026-10-06T08:56:52Z",
            "id": "5924209",
            "parentId": null,
            "replies": {
              "edges": [
                {
                  "node": {
                    "body": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/@patatruffe\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"\u003e@patatruffe\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;Thank you Romain! It definitely takes some courage to do a browser. We choose this form factor because we see agents as first-citizens. Chrome Extensions can only touch what's on browser and improve it, but we want to bring the agent capabilities into where people browse and have ideas. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWe're very thankful to the whole WebKit infrastructure. Without it, Rill won't be possible. We've done some technical deep dive into Chromium and I can tell you it's crazy down there. \u003c/p\u003e",
                    "createdAt": "2026-10-06T09:29:11Z",
                    "id": "5924312",
                    "parentId": "5924209",
                    "url": "https://www.producthunt.com/products/rill-3?comment=5924312\u0026utm_campaign=producthunt-api\u0026utm_medium=api-v2\u0026utm_source=Application%3A+sokel+%28ID%3A+304976%29",
