        {
          "node": {
            "body": "\u003cp\u003eHow is this different from Atlas, Comet or Dia? They all put AI next to the page.\u003c/p\u003e",
            "createdAt": "2026-10-06T08:41:57Z",
            "id": "5924153",
            "parentId": null,
            "replies": {
              "edges": [
                {
                  "node": {
                    "body": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/@justin2025\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"\u003e@justin2025\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;Great question Justin! We're fundamentally different from all of them because we treat AI agents as first citizens. \u003cbr\u003eThose \"AI browsers\" have a lot of cute functions that uses AI to improve your browsing, but they don't help with the actual heavy lifting that coding agents are doing today - run 1 week straight to solve a research problem, run 4 hours to create a great motion graphics video, go through 2000 old excel sheets with manual errors and sort all of them together. These are all things you can do with Astra and Fable today, and these are also things you can ask Rill to work on.  \u003cbr\u003eWe have deep respect for that incredible capability coding agents bring, so we see browsing not as something to be dramatically improved with AI gimmicks, but as the starting point of innovative ideas that can lead to real building. \u003c/p\u003e",
                    "createdAt": "2026-10-06T09:48:18Z",
                    "id": "5924381",
                    "parentId": "5924153",
                    "url": "https://www.producthunt.com/products/rill-3?comment=5924381\u0026utm_campaign=producthunt-api\u0026utm_medium=api-v2\u0026utm_source=Application%3A+sokel+%28ID%3A+304976%29",
                    "user": {
