          "node": {
            "body": "\u003cp\u003eNo Chrome extensions is a real cost for me, mostly the password manager. Just curious are people using this as the daily driver or as a second browser?\u003c/p\u003e",
            "createdAt": "2026-10-06T08:39:29Z",
            "id": "5924135",
            "parentId": null,
            "replies": {
              "edges": [
                {
                  "node": {
                    "body": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/@polman_trudo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"\u003e@polman_trudo\u003c/a\u003eWhat password manager do you use? Right now we use Mac's keychain to save the passwords, and have enabled importing Chrome and other browsers' password into it. Happy to support 3rd party password manager as well. \u003cbr\u003eChrome extensions are definitely great. One feature we'll launch in the future is \"Make your own extension\". The top left beautiful painting island is actually reserved for that. This way you're able to create your own extension with one simple ask, and customize them however you want. \u003c/p\u003e",
                    "createdAt": "2026-10-06T09:38:59Z",
                    "id": "5924351",
